### Step 1: Update Java Backend to send the Role Name
In your VoucherRequestServiceImpl.java, update the getWorkflowSteps method we created earlier so it performs a LEFT JOIN on your ROLES table. This replaces the raw ID with the actual name.
**REPLACE YOUR EXISTING getWorkflowSteps WITH THIS:**
```java
    public List<Map<String, Object>> getWorkflowSteps(String workflowCode) {
        // Advanced Join: Fetches the Role Name instead of just the ID
        String sql = "SELECT w.NEXT_STATE, w.CURRENT_ROLE_ID, r.ROLE_NAME " +
                     "FROM WORKFLOW_TRANSITIONS w " +
                     "LEFT JOIN ROLES r ON w.CURRENT_ROLE_ID = r.ROLE_ID " +
                     "WHERE w.WORKFLOW_CODE = ? AND w.ACTION_TAKEN IN ('CREATE', 'ACCEPTED') " +
                     "ORDER BY w.TRANSITION_ID ASC";
                     
        return jdbcTemplate.query(sql, (rs, rowNum) -> {
            Map<String, Object> step = new HashMap<>();
            String state = rs.getString("NEXT_STATE");
            step.put("state", state);
            step.put("label", state.replace("_", " ")); // e.g., "PENDING L1"
            
            // Send the actual Role Name! (Fallback to "System" if null)
            String roleName = rs.getString("ROLE_NAME");
            step.put("role", roleName != null ? roleName : "System Execution");
            return step;
        }, workflowCode);
    }

```
